# Filter - a filter you can play, rather than one you set.
#
# Cutoff, resonance and a mode are the classic part. The two extras are what
# moves it: `lfodepth` sweeps it in time with the transport, and `envdepth`
# follows the level of what is going through - and either can be negative, so
# the sweep can go down as things get louder, which is the setting that turns
# an auto-wah into something else.
#
# Families: fixed, sweep, extreme.

machine fx.Filter

patch Init family=fixed

patch "Low Cut" family=fixed
  # A high pass with no movement: everything under two hundred hertz gone. The
  # least exciting patch in the bank and the one most likely to be used.
  mode           #1
  cutoff         200 Hz
  reso           0.1
  gain           5.9 dB

patch Band family=fixed
  # A band pass in the middle, wide enough to leave the sound recognisable.
  # What a filter does when you want less of something rather than none.
  mode           #2
  cutoff         900 Hz
  reso           0.35
  gain           9.5 dB

patch Telephone family=fixed
  # Narrow, resonant, and centred where speech is. Everything above and below
  # is gone; what is left is the part a phone would have carried.
  mode           #2
  cutoff         1400 Hz
  reso           0.7
  gain           9.3 dB

patch "Auto Wah" family=sweep
  # The envelope opens it: loud parts are bright, quiet parts are dark. The
  # classic funk setting, and it works on anything with dynamics - a drum loop
  # more than a pad.
  cutoff         420 Hz
  reso           0.6
  envdepth       0.75

patch "Reverse Wah" family=sweep
  # The same follower with its sign turned round, so it *closes* as things get
  # louder. Nothing acoustic behaves this way and it is the more interesting
  # half of the control.
  cutoff         3000 Hz
  reso           0.55
  envdepth       -0.7

patch "Slow Sweep" family=sweep
  # Two bars a cycle, low resonance, wide range: the filter as a slow tide
  # rather than an effect. Long enough that you stop noticing it and only hear
  # that the loop is not repeating.
  cutoff         800 Hz
  reso           0.25
  lforate        #6
  lfodepth       0.85

patch Scream family=extreme
  # Resonance at the top, where the filter is nearly ringing on its own, swept
  # fast. The resonance is the sound and whatever went in is just exciting it.
  cutoff         600 Hz
  # Just under where it rings on its own. At 0.97 it peaked seven decibels
  # over full scale, which is not a patch, it is a fault with a name.
  reso           0.88
  lforate        #2
  lfodepth       0.6

patch Rhythmic family=extreme
  # Sixteenths, deep, resonant: the filter becomes the rhythm. On a held chord
  # it makes a part that was not played.
  cutoff         500 Hz
  reso           0.72
  lforate        #0
  lfodepth       0.9
  envdepth       0.3
